    "points": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "heading": "Practice -er",
        "body": "Comer is an infinitive in the Spanish -er family. Its stem is com-, and its present endings for yo, tú, and él are -o, -es, and -e.\n\nCom- plus -o makes yo como; plus -es makes tú comes; plus -e makes él come. Beber works in the same way: bebo, bebes, bebe.\n\nPractice: Conjugate beber and leer for yo, tú, and él. Write one sentence with él bebe.\n\nCommon mistake: Do not use -as from cantar here. T comes ends in -es."
      }
    ],
    "summary": ""
  },
